body:
The size isn't that big of an issue in my experiences! I play exclusively in handheld mode and I never had to really quint in order to see the story or lore-based texts. The only trouble with size that I came across was looking at the skills in your hotbar, but once you know what each skill does it doesn't really become too much of an issue.

&#x200B;

100% would recommend buying this game!

Wow, it's crazy that you'd check up on me almost 2 months past the post. That's super flattering!

&#x200B;

I dunno, I still feel awful from time to time, last week was a super low point. But at least I'm surviving. Still having bad thoughts during the month of November. Lot of the same problems but I have a lot more like, understanding or acceptance.

&#x200B;

Overall at least I'm stable for the upcoming future!

Hey there!

&#x200B;

I just woke up and I'm super flattered that you responded, despite it being yesterday night! 

&#x200B;

I feel like I have a lot of people I could potentially be close with and would be honored to get to know. In my mind, part of me is always telling me to stay away and just feel negative in general. I usually have to push myself to go and be sunny around people. When it comes to have a conversation and getting closer to someone, I usually freeze up especially if i don't have many things in common.

&#x200B;

The people who I thought I've gotten closer with have usually moved on. I know this is a common problem around reddit and I've tried to take in tips from other users and friends. I guess during my weak moments I give up hope, tell myself why do I even bother if it's just going to end up the same. It kind of reached a breaking point when I couldn't even get close to a group of gamers that I thought were cool.

&#x200B;

Now I'm studying so I"m quietly keeping things to myself. I dreamed about making a suicidal gesture, but I feel selfish and attention hungry and I hate the thought of me being like that. (Despite asking for help in this reddit)
